<h3>The 1000 TPS result</h3>
<p>Stacking all three layers on 8 H200 GPUs, the MiMo + TileRT deployment breaks <strong>1000 tokens/second</strong> decode throughput on a 1-trillion-parameter model under standard inference conditions. For comparison, serving a 1T-parameter model autoregressively on the same hardware achieves roughly 80–100 tokens/second — DFlash + FP4 + TileRT delivers approximately a 10× end-to-end speedup at 3× the cost of standard MiMo pricing.</p>

<div class="callout">
  <div class="callout-title">Why This Matters</div>
  <p>Previous paths to &gt;1000 TPS on trillion-parameter models required specialized silicon (like Groq's LPU) or massive multi-node deployments. MiMo 2.5 Pro UltraSpeed achieves this on commodity 8-GPU servers by combining algorithmic acceleration (DFlash), precision reduction (FP4), and kernel engineering (TileRT) — a recipe that scales with available hardware.</p>
