<p>The acceptance length variance across task types reflects a fundamental property of the diffusion drafter: the more structured and predictable the token distribution (code has rigid syntax, math has constrained symbols), the more accurately the drafter can fill the mask in one shot. Conversational text has higher entropy, reducing acceptance length to 3–4 — still a significant speedup over pure autoregressive decoding.</p>
